{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Submodule.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Abel"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation.sub_mem_finite_of_leading_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation.sub_mem_finite_of_leading_eq","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/MobiusLeadingCancellation.lean#L65-L74","doc":"**The Möbius application direction.** Two `ord ≤ 1` elements with the\n*same* leading coefficient `c` (the shared `c·ω` divergence of `I₁`,\n`I₂` in `rem:mobius-surreal-renormalization`) have finite difference —\nthe `ω^{+1}` parts cancel. Requires no independence hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation.sub_mem_finite_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation.sub_mem_finite_iff","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/MobiusLeadingCancellation.lean#L41-L63","doc":"**Leading-coefficient cancellation.** For `ord ≤ 1` elements\n`a • Ω + f` and `b • Ω + g` (with `f, g` finite), the difference is\nfinite iff the leading coefficients agree: `[Ω](I₁) = [Ω](I₂)`.\nThis is the algebraic content of the Möbius surreal renormalization's\nfiniteness bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation.IndependentOfFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.MobiusLeadingCancellation.IndependentOfFinite","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/MobiusLeadingCancellation.lean#L35-L39","doc":"The infinite unit `Ω` is independent of the finite part `F`: no nonzero\nscalar multiple of `Ω` is finite. In the surreal application `Ω` plays\n`ω^{+1}` and `F` the finite (`ord_ω ≤ 0`) elements. ","signatureChunk":0}]}